drawl -- English to Texan=========================    drawlA stdin-to-stdout filter that gives text a broad Texan accent: it dropsthe g from -ing, stretches and flattens vowels, and swaps in `tuh', `thuh'and the like.  Pipe any text through it:    echo "I am going to the store." | drawl    drawl < READMEAdam Hudd's English-to-Texan translator, from the `silly' collection postedto Usenet; a lex program, its scanner generated here with the disk's ownflex from drawl.l (in SRC/drawl/ORIG).